\code{"2013"} vintage, those of 2011 the \code{"2011"} vintage and those of 2001 the
\code{"2001"} vintage, so \code{\link[=pt_recode]{pt_recode()}} converts them to today's map. The 1991
census used an earlier map (4208 freguesias in 305 municípios, before
Odivelas, Trofa and Vizela were created in 1998), which geopt has no
vintage for.

Name-based \code{freguesia} scoping resolves against the current registry and,
for 2021, also matches through \code{\link[=pt_crosswalk]{pt_crosswalk()}}; for older censuses pass
that era's codes if a name does not resolve. In the 2001 files, two
freguesias still carry the code of the municipality they belonged to before
a transfer: Vale de Amoreira is \code{090756} (Guarda, now Manteigas) and Moita
\code{100117} (Alcobaça, now Marinha Grande). \code{\link[=pt_recode]{pt_recode()}} and \code{\link[=pt_match]{pt_match()}}
accept those codes for the \code{"2001"} vintage, and a \code{freguesia} filter finds
either form.
